      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon didn’t talk about Jesse Baird to friend in lead-up to alleged murders, court hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/07/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-friend-nicole-harvell-no-mention-jesse-baird-before-alleged-murders-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>NSW police officer has pleaded not guilty to murdering his ex and Luke Davies in a Sydney terrace in February 2024</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Despite an alleged obsession with his ex, Beau Lamarre-Condon never spoke about him to a close friend in the three months before allegedly murdering him, a jury has heard.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon, 31, has pleaded not guilty to murdering his ex-partner Jesse Baird and the man’s new boyfriend Luke Davies in a Sydney terrace in February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/07/beau-lamarre-condon-trial-friend-nicole-harvell-no-mention-jesse-baird-before-alleged-murders-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-07T02:45:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Privacy watchdog launches probe into China-based company behind Kmart ‘pervert glasses’ app",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/07/privacy-regulator-probe-kmart-anko-meta-smartglasses-australia",
      "description": "<p>Commissioner said Shenzhen Qingcheng, the app maker behind the HeyCyan app in the smartglasses, failed to respond to her inquiries</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Australian privacy regulator has opened an investigation into the China-based software company behind the HeyCyan app in Kmart’s $89 smartglasses, following public outrage over the covert use of the devices.</p><p>In August, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/04/kmart-camera-glasses-anko-meta-smartglasses-australia\">Guardian Australia reported</a> Kmart had sold out of the Anko-branded discount version of Meta’s smartglasses that can capture images and record high-definition video, which led to widespread concern and calls to ban or restrict their use.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/07/privacy-regulator-probe-kmart-anko-meta-smartglasses-australia\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-07T02:00:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hunter Valley community group wins landmark high court climate change case over Mount Pleasant coalmine",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/07/mount-pleasant-coalmine-case-high-court-climate-change-hunter-valley",
      "description": "<p>Ruling on Mount Pleasant coalmine shows ‘we cannot continue to dig up coal … and pretend the consequences have nothing to do with us’, group says</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A Hunter Valley community group has won Australia’s first high court case to consider climate change, in a ruling advocates say sets a binding national precedent for fossil fuel projects in New South Wales.</p><p>In a landmark judgment, the nation’s highest court ruled that the approval of MACH Energy’s Mount Pleasant coalmine expansion in Musswellbrook was invalid.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/07/mount-pleasant-coalmine-case-high-court-climate-change-hunter-valley\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-07T01:44:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comedian Dave Hughes to stop speaking at Liberal party events over political donation concerns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/07/comedian-dave-hughes-liberal-party-donation-law-concerns-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Entertainer alleges complaint made about ‘in-kind’ donations over Victorian fundraisers, where he has been railing against Labor</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Dave Hughes says he will no longer be taking the stage at Victorian Liberal events, claiming the party decided having him on the bill could run afoul of the state’s political donation laws.</p><p>The comedian, better known as Hughesy, once described himself as a lifelong Labor voter, but has become a vocal critic of the party following May’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/australian-budget-2026\">federal budget</a>, which included <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/may/12/australia-federal-budget-2026-tax-reform-capital-gains-cgt-changes-negative-gearing-housing-first-time-home-buyers-investors-explained\">sweeping reforms to negative gearing</a> and capital gain tax concessions.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/07/comedian-dave-hughes-liberal-party-donation-law-concerns-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-07T01:17:22"
    }
